- op: discuss  # e4f0
  at: '2026-08-28T21:01:08Z'  # e4f0
  by: agent  # e4f0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e4f0
  clock: 7  # e4f0
  nonce: e4f0  # e4f0
  message: "DONE via WI-surun, PR #613 (branch tip a99b4fae, CI success).\n\nTHE STATEMENT, ANSWERED IN ITS OWN TERMS -- \"One catalogue-scope rule, one gate\nshape applied to every language, and every asserting string agreeing with it.\"\n\nONE RULE. ADR-0016 s27 stands for the catalogues; ADR-0047 ruling 1 adds the\nthird state beside them (shipped, unvouched, disclosed). The rule now has NO\nexceptions left to cite: django.db.models was the last documented carve-out and\nthe owner ruled it moves with the rest.\n\nONE GATE SHAPE, ALL 15. packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_catalogue_scope_gates.py\nreplaces the 6-of-14 coverage this item measured. Three properties matter more\nthan the count:\n  - ALLOWLIST, not denylist. Three of the six originals named third-party\n    modules and asserted absence -- a hardcoded inventory that a NEW module\n    walks straight through, which is how execabs and grpc arrived in a\n    catalogue whose header said stdlib-only.\n  - THE TABLE IS THE CURATED LIST this item said lives nowhere but its own\n    prose. Selection and enforcement are now ONE artifact, each entry\n    carrying its reasoning, so the next stdlib climb cannot re-create the\n    drift silently.\n  - THE LANGUAGE LIST IS DERIVED FROM io_primitives/*.yaml, not restated.\n    That also closed a live hole this item did not name: CATALOG_LANGUAGES\n    hardcodes 14 while the tree ships 15, so bash.yaml sat outside it AND\n    outside the WI-sugav subprocess drift guard it feeds.\n\nTHE ROWS: 293 moved (elixir 144, haskell 43, swift 38, go 33, python 33).\nLOSSLESS AND CHECKED: across all 15 catalogues, catalogue+overlays is row-for-row\nidentical to before, with one intended deletion (erlang http_client, a phantom\nnaming no OTP module; removed on positive evidence -- 0 matches on ejabberd and\nemqx against httpc's 10 and 9).\n\nTHE ASSERTING STRINGS. Three catalogue headers that ADVERTISED third-party scope\nwere rewritten rather than left contradicting their contents (swift, haskell,\nelixir); docs/hypergumbo-spec.md 117 replaced its now-false \"third-party ... not\nshipped in-tree; a user supplies them\" with the shipped/unvouched/disclosed\nstate; docs/hypergumbo-self-catalog/README.md gained layer 1b. The CLI help\nneeded no change and is now TRUE for the first time.\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ITEM'S CENSUS: elixir is 144, not 155 (the gate first\nreported 145 because http_client is inherited from the erlang parent and counted\ntwice). go 33, swift 38 and python 33 matched exactly. haskell is 43 after my\nown INV-nular removals earlier the same day.\n\nMEASURED BEFORE SHIPPING (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/surun_ab_08282026/RESULT.md):\ndefault runs UNCHANGED on all five cohort repos; --no-default-overlays reports\nless as predicted (pretix -846 edges / -70.4%, plausible -139 / -26.9%). The\nverdict zero (0 of 20 moved) is NOT quotable -- the cohort held no `confirmed`\nverdict, the only value that can degrade. A positive control shows the real\ncost: confirmed rc 0 -> inconclusive rc 2 for a repo whose external calls land\nin a relocated module.\n\nFull suite 24,585 passed / 0 failed; mypy ratchet clean."  # e4f0
